/* ---------------------------------------------------------------
   THE LIBRARY — every line we know about for the two openings, with
   where it comes from and how much weight it carries.

   This is the single source of truth for moves, sources, notes and
   plans. The app drills only the lines that tools/repertoire.seed.mjs
   SELECTS by id (weight A/B, no conflicting alternatives, no engine
   moves); everything else here is research to recognise, not to drill.
   `plan` / `planSources`: what to do when the line ends, in the words
   of the cited source — shown in the app at the end of a drilled line.

   weight (how much the line can be trusted):
     A  theory — in a dedicated book / MCO / masters' main practice
     B  known  — taught in a course or by a titled player on video,
                 or named in Wikipedia with a citation
     C  community — Lichess studies, forum posts (unverified by a title)
     E  engine — only Stockfish says so
   kind:
     main  — a sound choice by the opponent you must know
     side  — an inferior move with a known answer
     trap  — a forcing trick (works only if the opponent cooperates)
     alt   — an alternative for OUR side (not our repertoire move, but
             theory you should recognise)
   Sources are keyed into SOURCES below. `moves` are SAN from move 1 and
   are checked for legality by tests/library.test.mjs.
--------------------------------------------------------------- */

